Subject: [PATCH] tvm-ffi: -Xcompiler takes ONE argument, so /O2 became an input file

apache-tvm-ffi builds an nvcc command line that nvcc refuses, on Windows only,
and it blocks every JIT kernel FreeToken compiles at startup. Measured on the
Dell (Windows 11, CUDA 12.6, RTX 3050) on 2026-09-25 with
apache-tvm-ffi==0.1.13.post3, which pyproject.toml pins.

WHAT HAPPENS. `-Xcompiler` forwards ONE argument to the host compiler. Given
["-Xcompiler", "/std:c++17", "/O2"], nvcc hands /std:c++17 to cl.exe and is left
holding /O2 as a free token, which it reads as a SECOND input file:

    nvcc fatal : A single input file is required for a non-link phase when an
                 outputfile is specified

The engine dies with that, on freetoken__index_3072_2_128_1_false_*, after the
weights have already loaded -- so it looks like a runtime fault rather than a
build one: /v1/models answers 200, and the first real generation returns 503.

REPRODUCED IN ONE LINE, not inferred. With a .cu containing only
`__global__ void k(){}`:

    -Xcompiler /std:c++17 /O2   -> nvcc fatal: A single input file is required
                                   (character for character, the engine's error)
    -Xcompiler /std:c++17,/O2   -> passes argument parsing

WINDOWS ONLY, and that is why nobody has hit it. The Linux branch of the same
function (line ~427) is ["-std=c++17", "-O2"] with no -Xcompiler, because there
it is not needed. This patch touches the Windows branch alone, so a Linux node
applying it changes nothing.

NOT FIXED BY UPGRADING, and not avoidable from our side. Checked, not assumed:
0.1.14.post1 -- the latest -- carries the identical line 418. And
extension.py:450 does `cuda_cflags = default_cuda_cflags + extra_cuda_cflags`:
it SUMS, so anything FreeToken passes is appended and the free token stays.

WHY A VERSIONED PATCH AND NOT AN EDIT IN THE VENV. Editing the installed file
works tonight and makes that machine differ from a clean install WITHOUT IT
BEING VISIBLE -- which is the class of invisible divergence that undermines
exactly the cross-node comparability these measurements exist for. A patch in
the repository means a clean install REBUILDS the same divergence instead of
not having it: a machine that differs in a declared way. The MacBook Air M2
already carries patches/llama.cpp-moestream-metrics.patch for the same reason.

UPSTREAM: not yet reported at the time of writing. Put the link here when it is,
and delete this file when a released version carries the fix.

--- a/tvm_ffi/cpp/extension.py
+++ b/tvm_ffi/cpp/extension.py
@@ -415,7 +415,7 @@
         ]
         default_cflags += _win_warnings
         default_cxxflags += _win_warnings
-        default_cuda_cflags = ["-Xcompiler", "/std:c++17", "/O2"]
+        default_cuda_cflags = ["-Xcompiler", "/std:c++17,/O2"]
         default_ldflags = [
             "/DLL",
             f"/LIBPATH:{tvm_ffi_lib_path}",
